# 📘 DARS 223: PRESENT PERFECT — I HAVE DONE

## 🤖 TalkMe (TTS matni)

> Salom yana! Bugun biz **Present Perfect** — “hozirgi tugallangan” — ni o‘rganamiz. Bu — **o‘tgan zamonda boshlanib, hozirgi zamon bilan bog‘liq** bo‘lgan ish-harakat. **Natija** hozir ko‘z oldimizda. “Men kalitimni **yo‘qotdim**” — “I **have lost** my key”. (Hozir kalitim yo‘q.) Qo‘rqmang! 🚀

## 📖 QOIDA

**Present Perfect** — o‘tgan harakat, natija hozir.

**Yasalishi:** **have/has + Past Participle (P.P.)**.

> I **have worked** — men ishladim (natija hozir).
> He **has worked** — u ishladi.
> They **have worked** — ular ishladilar.

**Bo‘lishsiz:** haven’t/hasn’t + P.P. → I **haven’t worked**.
**So‘roq:** Have/Has + ega + P.P.? → **Have** you **worked**?

**Qachon ishlatamiz?**
> Natijasi hozir ko‘rinib turgan: I **have broken** my pencil. (Qalamim siniq — hozir ham.)
> Hayot davomida takrorlangan: I **have seen** this film three times.
> Hali tugamagan vaqt: I **have read** two books **today**.
> **Since/for** bilan: I **have lived** here **since** 2020 / **for** five years.
> **Just, already, yet, ever, never** bilan: I **have just** finished.

**Muhim:** Present Perfect **aniq o‘tgan zamon** bilan ishlatilmaydi: ❌ I have seen him **yesterday**. → ✅ I **saw** him yesterday.

## 💬 MISOLLAR

> I **have lost** my key. — Men kalitimni yo‘qotdim. (Hozir kalitim yo‘q.)
> She **has just left**. — U hozirgina ketdi.
> **Have** you **ever been** to Paris? — Siz Parijda bo‘lganmisiz?
> I **have never eaten** sushi. — Men hech qachon sushi yemaganman.
> He **hasn’t finished** his homework **yet**. — U hali uy vazifasini tugatmagan.
> We **have known** each other **for** ten years. — Biz bir-birimizni o‘n yildan buyon taniymiz.

## ✍️ MASHQ

